{
  "slug": "html_tables",
  "course": "html",
  "order": 25,
  "url": "/html/html_tables.asp",
  "title": "HTML Tables",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "HTML Tables"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "HTML tables allow web developers to arrange data into rows and\ncolumns."
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_table_intro"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Define an HTML Table"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "A table in HTML consists of table cells inside rows and columns."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "html",
      "text": "<table>\n\n<tr>\n    <th>Company</th>\n\n    <th>Contact</th>\n    <th>Country</th>\n\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n    <td>Alfreds Futterkiste</td>\n\n    <td>Maria\n  Anders</td>\n    <td>Germany</td>\n\n</tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>Centro\n  comercial Moctezuma</td>\n\n    <td>Francisco\n  Chang</td>\n    <td>Mexico</td>\n\n  </tr>\n</table>",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_table3"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Table Cells"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Each table cell is defined by a\n<td> and a </td> tag."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "variant": "note",
      "text": "td\nstands for table data."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Everything between <td> and </td>\nis the content of a table cell."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "html",
      "text": "<table>\n\n<tr>\n    <td>Emil</td>\n\n    <td>Tobias</td>\n    <td>Linus</td>\n\n</tr>\n</table>",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_table4"
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "variant": "note",
      "text": "A table cell can contain\nall sorts of HTML elements: text, images, lists, links, other tables, etc."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Table Rows"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Each table row starts with a\n<tr> and ends with a </tr> tag."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "variant": "note",
      "text": "tr\nstands for table row."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "html",
      "text": "<table>\n\n<tr>\n    <td>Emil</td>\n\n    <td>Tobias</td>\n    <td>Linus</td>\n\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n    <td>16</td>\n\n    <td>14</td>\n    <td>10</td>\n\n</tr>\n</table>",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_table5"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "You can have as many rows as you like in a table; just make sure that the number of cells are the same in each row."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "variant": "note",
      "text": "There are times when a row can have fewer or more cells than another. You will learn about that in a later chapter."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Table Headers"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Sometimes you want your cells to be table header cells. In those cases use the\n<th> tag instead of the\n<td> tag:"
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "variant": "note",
      "text": "th\nstands for table header."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "html",
      "text": "<table>\n\n<tr>\n    <th>Person 1</th>\n\n    <th>Person 2</th>\n    <th>Person\n  3</th>\n\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n    <td>Emil</td>\n\n    <td>Tobias</td>\n    <td>Linus</td>\n\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n    <td>16</td>\n\n    <td>14</td>\n    <td>10</td>\n\n</tr>\n</table>",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_table6"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "By default, the text in <th> elements\nare bold and centered, but you can change that with CSS."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "HTML Table Tags"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "headers": ["Tag", "Description"],
      "rows": [
        ["<table>", "Defines a table"],
        ["<th>", "Defines a header cell in a table"],
        ["<tr>", "Defines a row in a table"],
        ["<td>", "Defines a cell in a table"],
        ["<caption>", "Defines a table caption"],
        ["<colgroup>", "Specifies a group of one or more columns in a table for formatting"],
        ["<col>", "Specifies column properties for each column within a <colgroup> element"],
        ["<thead>", "Groups the header content in a table"],
        ["<tbody>", "Groups the body content in a table"],
        ["<tfoot>", "Groups the footer content in a table"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "variant": "note",
      "text": "For a complete list of all available HTML tags, visit our HTML Tag Reference."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "LEARN MORE"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Styling Tables\nFilter Table\nSort Table\nResponsive Table\nZebra Striped Table"
    }
  ]
}
